  "interpretation": "Distance remains an excellent predictor in this deliberately local field, but response-update overlap is not merely a relabeling of distance. Output-subspace overlap predicts log non-additivity better than a distance-only linear fit in this frozen panel (R^2 0.9923 versus 0.9743), and two-sided overlap remains strongly correlated with interference after subtracting the mean of each exact-distance group (r 0.8371). This suggests the portable hypothesis that physical separation protects edits because it separates the response-geometry patches they occupy.",
  "limitations": [
    "one deterministic PhiWorld-like field and one response basis",
    "34 deliberately geometry-stratified pairs, not an independent random population",
    "overlap and non-additivity share the same simulated operator measurement machinery",
    "correlation is not a causal proof that subspace overlap creates the interaction",
    "no adaptive learner or biological growth mechanism is implemented here"
  ],
